Search on Cover, and Feedback moves to the side menu — 18 Sept.

Ali: "theres no search button on the consultants page" · "on phone if search and resident merge
how do you see which resitned are on. needs a rethink" · "take the feedback out add resident
iicon into top on phone".

THE RETHINK. Residents is NOT a list — it sets showJun and redraws the residents INSIDE each pod
cell. It is a layer on the board. So it cannot live behind a search sheet, and my earlier
suggestion that it could was wrong. It stays exactly where it was, on the phone, in the header.

  before   Residents · Feedback · Key · Edit
  after    Residents · Search   · Key · Edit        Feedback in the side menu

Feedback is the one of the four that is not about the day in front of you, and in the side menu
it sits beside Pods and Fairness — open to everyone, nothing moved behind the shield. Two tests
assert exactly that: it is in `aside`, it is NOT in `#teamPanel`, and it still opens the same
dialog.

THE SEARCH SHEET answers WHO and never redraws the board — a test asserts the week grid's HTML
is byte-identical after opening it, because "search does not do Residents' job" is the whole
point of the rethink. Type a name, a pod or a skill, or tap one of five skill chips, each
carrying a count. Consultants come from the map; residents and their skills from the resident
board's staff list, which this page already loads to draw the pods — so echo accreditation is
searchable here for free.

It reads the week ON SCREEN, not today: today when today is in that week, that week's Monday
when it is not. Somebody looking at next week is asking about next week.

Tests: render 66 passed / 0 failed (five new) · chip-probe 80/0 · attn-probe 19/0.
The stale toolbar assertion was updated rather than deleted — btnFeedback left that set on
purpose, btnFind took its place, and the comment says so.
